# Monorepo rule scope (subapps)

This repository is an **Nx / workspace monorepo**. Cursor rules under `.cursor/rules/` are **not** root-only chrome.

## Where rules apply

Treat every **child project** as an app that must follow these rules:

| Kind | Paths | Examples |
| ---- | ----- | -------- |
| Subapps (MF host + checked-out remotes) | `apps/*` | `apps/shell`, `apps/<remote>` (polyrepo checkout) |
| Shared packages / libs | `packages/*` | `packages/ui`, `packages/mf-config`, `packages/auth` |

When an agent scaffolds, refactors, or reviews code:

1. Apply architecture, hook, UI/logic-split, and naming rules **inside each child** (`apps/<name>/…`, `packages/<name>/…`).
2. Do **not** assume rules only cover the workspace root or a single `src/` at repo root.
3. Each subapp owns its own `src/` tree; feature/page/hook layout rules map onto **that** project’s `src/`, not a fictional monorepo-wide `src/`.
4. Shared packages (`packages/*`) follow the same separation and naming rules; they are still “children” of this repo.
5. Remotes are **polyrepo**: only `apps/shell` is committed to platform; other `apps/*` come from `bun run pull-remote`.

## Mental model

```txt
sale-platform-shoniz/          ← platform git (shell + packages + tools)
  apps/shell/                  ← host — RULES APPLY HERE
  apps/<remote>/               ← optional local clone — RULES APPLY HERE
  packages/ui/                 ← shared — RULES APPLY HERE
  .cursor/rules/               ← agent rules for all children above
```

If unsure whether a rule applies: **yes, if the file lives under `apps/*` or `packages/*`.**
